<p>Taiwan opposition leader and Kuomintang chair Cheng Li-wun arrived in Shanghai on Tuesday for a six-day trip to mainland China, calling it a &quot;journey for peace&quot; and a chance to serve as a &quot;bridge for peace&quot; across the Taiwan Strait. The visit, made at the invitation of Chinese President Xi Jinping, is the first by a Taiwan opposition leader to China since 2016 and comes as Beijing continues to press its claim over the self-governed island. Cheng said she hopes the trip can help make the Taiwan Strait safer, rather than one of the world’s &quot;most dangerous places,&quot; though her planned meeting with Xi has drawn scrutiny in Taipei as cross-strait tensions remain high. Even so, the visit is a rare moment of direct high-level contact at a time when Taiwan’s major parties sharply disagree on how to manage relations with Beijing.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CNXM41nFvjmtI5Z0NOd7a0UwzCgo7Tjep_0W--SO5ii4L43Mqpm7XF5U1B21E-Cke6EuA_T2CLfbyyuoMLonY3enl3pkwXaCmMadzrEuZ6RrFW7rsQ2wUwom5XHziMOiBLcv3m07QSYW7mOcHdSG5ptkj3E6SIk-MFO094mm_w' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Delegation makeup: Cheng is leading a 14-member delegation, including three KMT vice-chairmen, on the mainland trip.</li></ul><blockquote>Gladly accepted - Cheng Li-wun</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637489-taiwan-opposition-visit-to-china/'>Taiwan opposition leader heads to China</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/taiwan-opposition-leader-heads-china-calls-journey-peace-131789103'>Taiwan opposition leader heads to China in what she calls a ‘journey for peace’</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3349225/taiwanese-opposition-leader-cheng-li-wun-begins-journey-peace-shanghai'>Taiwanese opposition leader Cheng Li-wun begins ‘journey of peace’ in Shanghai</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c0krnz7mmmjo'>Taiwan oppositi